{"id": "EUVD-2026-81821", "enisaUuid": "5c35050b-6b3d-3598-af78-8db431d457f6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvmet: fix NULL pointer dereference in nvmet_execute_identify_ns_zns()\n\nWhen a host issues an Identify command with CNS 05h (I/O Command Set\nspecific Identify Namespace) and CSI 02h (ZNS) targeting a file-backed\nnamespace, nvmet_execute_identify_ns_zns() calls bdev_is_zoned() on\nreq->ns->bdev. A file-backed namespace has no block device, so\nreq->ns->bdev is NULL and bdev_is_zoned() dereferences it, oopsing.\n\nThe I/O command set is selected by the host-supplied CSI field and the\ncommand is routed here whenever CONFIG_BLK_DEV_ZONED is enabled,\nindependent of the namespace backing type, so any file-backed namespace\nis exposed.\n\nReject the command with Invalid Field when the namespace is not backed\nby a block device.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:00:04", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ce8faf90eb0bf5599b90db38500aefea9426485", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b873099944dae5702b4b6db6814d1f1e8d4cfb00", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff28a93a895912010a7827a0e1445ebe8be53b4d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc29f7082b7ab5e0337f27d1fef16359f05fcffa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1fb1236312ee1a600de6b3ca560f0b3fd5a50471", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b4cf43f9ca7118590a338de900edbd6047cd89f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f594863967d87b7fcbff6e724d51135fd701a13d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90228", "GHSA-cxmg-vfm8-pw64"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.67, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0776714a-2e56-3fa4-b853-e26742b5f722", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "1486f9e7-86f8-3660-8e68-8d991a6b5950", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "29f87d55-96a4-33bd-a6cd-8cd0819c57ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaf2e048af2704da5869f27b508b288f36d5c7b7 <0b4cf43f9ca7118590a338de900edbd6047cd89f"}, {"id": "2f48be4a-6a0e-3766-b3dd-92c5bbd6a794", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "47197ba2-1e6f-3c88-8852-01eb4a216278", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "62163b09-bce5-320b-8be2-4ffd9570e4fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "68f698ad-376e-3c03-8fff-c4a1854510cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaf2e048af2704da5869f27b508b288f36d5c7b7 <b873099944dae5702b4b6db6814d1f1e8d4cfb00"}, {"id": "769f5c19-7bb5-33e5-acc7-55dce73cd956", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaf2e048af2704da5869f27b508b288f36d5c7b7 <1fb1236312ee1a600de6b3ca560f0b3fd5a50471"}, {"id": "84490802-031a-378c-a8b7-cdea417fda86", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "949f66ad-e2f5-3021-b187-9733b0c6f607", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaf2e048af2704da5869f27b508b288f36d5c7b7 <cc29f7082b7ab5e0337f27d1fef16359f05fcffa"}, {"id": "ad65f009-306a-3a95-b30d-8bd549f1fdc6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.14"}, {"id": "b643c886-8ac8-3672-a068-aff2ec11d86a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaf2e048af2704da5869f27b508b288f36d5c7b7 <1ce8faf90eb0bf5599b90db38500aefea9426485"}, {"id": "b7344332-6020-38af-9959-ea4a9280232a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaf2e048af2704da5869f27b508b288f36d5c7b7 <f594863967d87b7fcbff6e724d5113